  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. Switching FancyZones layouts while dragging a window with Shift held is tracked in PowerToys#14567, #4969 and #26720. Those tickets were closed as duplicates of each other, and the archive shows no implementation. Alt is not a built-in way to switch layouts today. Two things work now. First, you can assign a hotkey to each layout in the FancyZones editor and press Win+Ctrl+Alt+number to apply it. While you drag, a number key can switch layouts if the hotkey is set up. Second, you can enable the non-primary mouse button setting so you don't need to hold Shift. Users in #4969 posted an AutoHotkey script that cycles layouts with the scroll wheel or the mouse side buttons while dragging. Add a 👍 and your Alt idea to #14567 instead of opening a new ticket."
 },
